# =============================================================================
# CODEOWNERS — Porsche Design System
# =============================================================================
#
# Each line is a glob pattern followed by one or more owners (GitHub usernames
# or @org/team handles). The LAST matching pattern in this file is the one
# that takes effect for a given file.
#
# Owners listed here are automatically requested for review on PRs touching
# matching files. To make this enforceable, configure the branch protection
# rule (or ruleset) on `main` and `v4` to "Require review from Code Owners".
#
# Syntax notes:
#   - Patterns follow the same rules as .gitignore.
#   - "/foo"     → only `foo` at the repo root
#   - "foo/"     → any directory called `foo` anywhere
#   - "**/foo"   → `foo` at any depth
#   - Multiple owners are space-separated; ALL of them are notified, but
#     only ONE approval from any team member is required.
#
# Maintainership is managed via the GitHub team:
#   https://github.com/orgs/porsche-design-system/teams/maintainers
#
# To add or remove maintainers, change team membership in the GitHub UI —
# no edits to this file are required.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default owners — match anything not covered by a more specific rule below.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                       @porsche-design-system/maintainers


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# High-impact paths — explicit ownership for clarity, even though the default
# rule above already covers them. Listing them keeps intent obvious in code
# review and survives any future restructuring of the default line.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# CI/CD, GitHub config, this file itself.
/.github/                               @porsche-design-system/maintainers
/.github/workflows/                     @porsche-design-system/maintainers
/.github/CODEOWNERS                     @porsche-design-system/maintainers

# Security policy and root config.
/SECURITY.md                            @porsche-design-system/maintainers
/package.json                           @porsche-design-system/maintainers
/package-lock.json                      @porsche-design-system/maintainers
/biome.json                             @porsche-design-system/maintainers
/prettier.config.js                     @porsche-design-system/maintainers
/tsconfig*.json                         @porsche-design-system/maintainers

# Patches applied to upstream dependencies — security-sensitive.
/patches/                               @porsche-design-system/maintainers
